cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  INAUSIS — a chain-aligned magnetorheological elastomer and a causal
  Difference-of-Gaussians tactile front-end
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite the repository and the companion
  manuscript relevant to the part you used: the material paper for the
  elastomer and its dual-modal physics, the TTCGS paper for the
  signal-processing front-end.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Pin-Han
    family-names: Li
    email: sigmansslee@gmail.com
    city: Hsinchu
    country: TW
repository-code: 'https://github.com/sigmanssery/INAUSIS'
abstract: >-
  A biomimetic dual-modal tactile sensing front-end. A chain-aligned
  magnetorheological elastomer provides a field-emission piezoresistive
  readout below ~6 kPa and a permeability-coupled inductive readout above it,
  with the handover fixed by the vanishing of dR/dP rather than by design
  preference. A causal multi-scale Difference-of-Gaussians encoder with a
  z-score significance-flag engine runs the whole datapath on a single
  commodity FPGA at 27 MHz, transmitting an 18-dimensional feature vector and
  an attention mask over a single-wire Manchester link with a CRC-protected
  reverse channel.
keywords:
  - tactile sensing
  - magnetorheological elastomer
  - inductance-to-digital conversion
  - Difference-of-Gaussians
  - FPGA
  - neuromorphic front-end
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
